  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving the lives of Older Persons in Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1. Community-led initiatives are identified and analyzed based on the Participatory Action Learning in Crises methodology.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 2: Older people are supported through community-led initiatives funded through microgrants to enable the scale-up of self-help actions aimed at enhancing survival and recovery.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 3: Lessons learned are captured and shared.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will focus on supporting eight community-led initiatives by providing capacity building and microgrants to Self-Help Groups. The initiative will address the immediate needs of 1,600 Ukrainian men and women over the age of 60.</narrative>
  </description>
